A newer file came out (last modified 01:18 UTC on 5 November, 146 pages, 33 chapters), and I could measure it against today's chapters, so this replaces 065, whose chapter labels and figure counts rested on an older copy. How: I built the chapters as data in a scratch process, with the online-view builder's address gate switched off in that process only, into a scratch file, nothing written into the repository (security has the question about that chapter, developer__066, and will be told). Also, the 862 of 962 paragraphs placed that I gave in 064 and 065 were a fault of my matcher, not of the print: after one false early match the search pointer sat ahead of its chapter and passed over the rest of it (the words were on pages 12 to 15 while it looked from 16 on). Fixed with a look back; now 1000 of 1018 are placed, and all 101 figure lines are found by their caption.

